# Astraudit — local development environment template.
#
# Astraudit's runtime SPA does NOT read environment variables. The
# user-facing GitHub PAT lives in localStorage only and never hits
# any backend (because there is no backend).
#
# This file documents the env vars the *helper scripts* in
# `scripts/` honour during development. Copy this file to `.env`
# (gitignored) if you regularly run the audit harnesses against
# real GitHub repos.

# Optional. A fine-grained personal access token with `public_repo`
# read scope. Used by `scripts/test-audit.ts` and
# `scripts/validate-org-health.ts` to authenticate REST + raw
# requests so the suite can run past the 60 req/hr unauthenticated
# limit. The browser-based dashboard ignores this variable
# entirely; users supply their PAT via the in-app Settings dialog.
#
# DO NOT commit a real token. The `.env` file is gitignored.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Alias accepted by the same scripts. Either name works.
GH_TOKEN=
